{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"The user is asking me to:\n1. Get the total farmers markets (excluding territories) from a CSV file\n2. Get the 2025 population from a census file (using the 'United States' row)\n3. Calculate farmers markets per 100,000 residents\n4. Provide the answer to four decimal places\n5. Use tools to do the math and verification\n\nAccording to the project instructions (AGENTS.md), I should:\n1. First check if there's a semantic model or existing alias for this\n2. Use xorq_catalog to work with data\n3. Never fabricate numbers - always get them from expressions\n4. Use xorq_select for values and xorq_verify to verify them\n5. Create a formula/metric in the catalog if needed for the ratio\n\nLet me start by:\n1. Checking the semantic models in the catalog\n2. Checking the existing aliases\n3. Then ingest the two data sources if needed\n4. Calculate the metric\n\nLet me begin by orienting myself with the catalog."}}
